---
// Trust element for health-topic pages — establishes E-E-A-T signals
// (Experience, Expertise, Authoritativeness, Trustworthiness) that Google's
// Quality Rater Guidelines specifically call out for YMYL health content.
---

<aside class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 mt-10 mb-4">
  <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 bg-gray-50 text-sm">
    <h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
      <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="text-amber-600" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z" />
      </svg>
      Editorial standards
    </h2>
    <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
      All health content on this site is drawn from peer-reviewed primary literature and current
      clinical practice guidelines — principally the Institute of Medicine (2011), the Endocrine
      Society (2011), and cited randomised trials. Recommendations reflect published consensus
      thresholds and are not substitutes for individualised medical advice.
      See our <a href="/how-it-works" class="text-amber-700 underline">methodology page</a> for
      the full model and citation list.
    </p>
  </div>
</aside>
